  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreS&E 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team has conducted several preclinical animal studies and
    is considering whether this potential new cancer drug is ready to move into human
    trials.


    <b>Which group reviews the science to make sure the project is
    well designed and worth moving forward?</b>'
  explanation: The SRC reviews the scientific quality and feasibility of a study
    to ensure the research question makes sense and the methods are appropriate.
    They may suggest improvements or request changes, helping confirm the project
    is strong enough to move toward animal studies and future clinical steps.
  correctAnswer: Scientific Review Committee (SRC)
  incorrectAnswer1: Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC)
  incorrectAnswer2: Data and Safety Monitoring Board (DSMB)
  incorrectAnswer3: Food and Drug Administration (FDA)
  questionRole: Safety & Ethics
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: PreClinical
